From f536b3fa9bd2b451f8216e58bd9a6e832bcb8a78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: julian <julian@jc84.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 23:44:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] feat: configurable touch gestures
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add configurable touchscreen and touchpad gesture binds, integrated
into the unified binds {} block as parameterized KDL triggers:

- TouchSwipe / TouchPinch / TouchRotate / TouchTap / TouchTapHoldDrag
  fingers=N (3..=10) with direction properties, recognized by a new
  touchscreen gesture state machine (libinput exposes only raw touch
  points for touchscreens).
- TouchEdge edge="..." with optional zone="..." — single-finger edge
  swipes, each edge split into three zones with parent-bind fallback.
- TouchpadSwipe / TouchpadPinch / TouchpadTapHold / TouchpadTapHoldDrag
  driven by libinput's native gesture events (touchpad pinch allows
  fingers=2, matching libinput's 2-finger pinch support).
- Per-device tuning knobs under input.touchscreen.gestures and
  input.touchpad.gestures (trigger distances, tap wobble/timeout,
  tap-hold delay, rotation angles, dominance ratios).
- Continuous gestures drive workspace/overview animations with smooth
  progress; discrete gestures fire actions on threshold.
- noop action support for capturing gestures without an action
  (swallow a gesture instead of passing it to the client).
- touchscreen-gesture-passthrough window rule to exempt clients.
- Design doc: Design:-Touchscreen-Gestures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
